  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 101 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nWith the front stalled across Deep South Texas, there will be\ncontinuing chances for rain into the weekend. Rainfall totals \nwill continue to be more moderate. A few showers may linger into \nMonday. By Tuesday the front will have moved away and upper level \nridging will move back over Texas bringing dry weather back. With \ncloudy skies and scattered showers the long term period will start\noff cooler with highs in the 70s and 80s Saturday. From there \ntemperatures will slowly increase reaching the low to mid 80s by \nTuesday and staying there. These are about normal for this time of\nyear.",
